      "extract": "In \\cite{Sin88, KS22} it was shown that the Farey map $\\hat{\\mathscr{M}}_{3}$ is the universal triangular map. The Farey map is a map on the upper-half plane whose vertices are the extended rationals $\\mathbb{Q}\\cup \\{\\infty\\}$ and where two rationals $\\frac{a}{c}$ and $\\frac{b}{d}$ are joined by an edge if and only if $ad-bc=\\pm 1.$ We sometimes refer to the rational $\\frac{a}{c}$ as a {\\it Farey coordinate.} The",
