      ],
      "extract": "Farey fractions were first introduced in \\cite{SS19} for the case $q=3$. A Farey fraction modulo $n$ is a pair $(a,c)$ where $(a,c,n)=1$ and where we identify $\\frac{a}{c}$ with $\\frac{-a}{-c}.$ We think of these fractions as being points on $\\mathbb{H}/\\Gamma(n)$. Two Farey fractions mod $n$, $(a,c)$ and $ (b,d)$ are adjacent when $ad-bc\\equiv \\pm 1 \\; \\text{mod}\\;n$. \\begin{example} {$n=5.$} The Farey fractions",
