      "extract": "The main aim of this paper is to find Hecke-Farey fractions for Bring's curve, $\\mathscr{M}_4(5).$ In general, for a positive integer $n$ the map $\\mathcal{M}_4(n)$ has vertices of the form $\\frac{a}{\\sqrt 2 c}$ or $\\frac{b\\sqrt 2}{d}$. where $a,b,c,d\\in \\mathbb{Z}_n.$ These numbers are called {\\it Hecke-Farey coordinates.}These two vertices are joined by an edge If and only if $ad-2bc\\equiv \\pm 1$ mod$\\ n.$ Before",
